silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_03_pullback_vs_pushforward_sections_02_pullback_as_constraint_validation_concrete_anchor silm:hasExample "In 'PullbackAsConstraintValidationConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, the clinic-side SHACL shape that asserts every body-mass is in [0.5, 10] kg; also, a derived anchor for the transport diagram: the clinic-side image of the household typed leg, carrying composition data.." .
